## How I use AI

AI is an execution and acceleration layer inside operational system design — not the product.

**Where it earns its place:**

- Prompt engineering and workflow-logic generation
- Code scaffolding and rapid prototyping against unfamiliar DOMs
- Debugging and iteration cycles measured in minutes instead of hours
- Turning production failure telemetry into structured specifications
- **Building the tools AI operates** — the MCP layer above exists so an LLM can drive real operational systems directly, with the safety rails wired in

**Where it doesn't:** anything needing judgment on every item, anything that runs once, and
anything where being wrong is expensive and hard to undo. Those need deliberate design, and
the design is the job.

